  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Solve for $z$ where $3{z}^{2}-\\frac{25}{12}=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the ${z}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}-\\frac{25}{12} & =0 \\\\ 3{z}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{12} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{36}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
